Mechanical and Electrical Design of Hydroelectric Power Plants — USACE (@pe-usace: 0, is #reference, #part-of @pe-sources) { r_1N0D32HTSXMVJ1VRW9TNTYV9P8
U.S. Army Corps of Engineers. EM 1110-2-3006, Mechanical and Electrical Design of Hydroelectric Power Plants, 22 April 2024. [Official publication record](https://www.publications.usace.army.mil/USACE-Publications/Engineer-Manuals/u43544q/776169766572/) · [Complete official manual](https://www.publications.usace.army.mil/Portals/76/Publications/EngineerManuals/EM%201110-2-3006_2024Apr22.pdf).

Read the whole manual during the facility-design investigation, with sustained electrical generation, transformers, auxiliaries, switchgear, controls, protection, monitoring and mechanical-interface study. Follow a component from functional requirement through the complete plant design and rehabilitation context.

The official catalogue and indexed revision summary identify the title, date and merger of the older electrical and mechanical manuals; checked on 29 October 2026. Direct PDF retrieval returned 403, so complete-page inspection is not claimed. A summary-page date differs from the catalogue/footer date; retain the actual issued document rather than silently changing it. Public federal access and component rights remain distinct, and USACE-specific requirements are not universal installation rules. No manual or drawings are bundled.

**Return:** [Power-engineering sources — complete books, courses, methods and evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_12EFX00X7ZXGT9MPMJDYRTNY9N).
